FAQ
Questions people actually ask
Can I open my files from my computer's file manager?
Yes, through the sync app: the folders you add are ordinary folders on your computer, kept in sync with the device. What there isn't is a network drive (SMB) that opens the device's own storage directly, as a traditional NAS does.
Are my files private?
Yes. Your files are stored encrypted on the device's drives, with a key only your password unlocks, and the password itself is never stored on it. Each person in the family has their own account and key, and nothing is used for ads or to train AI.
What happens if a drive fails?
Nothing is lost: each of the two drives holds a full copy. The device carries on with the other one and tells you which to replace; put a new drive in its place and it copies everything back by itself.
How much space do I get?
As much as one of your two drives holds, since each keeps a full copy. To grow it, swap the drives for bigger ones, one at a time: the device copies everything onto each new drive, then grows by itself, without stopping.
